{"id":"long-way-down","title":"Long Way Down","who":"Ewan McGregor & Charley Boorman","when":"May–August 2007","vehicle":"BMW R1200GS Adventure","kind":"moto","color":"#b91c1c","summary":"From the northern tip of Scotland to Cape Town: down through Europe, across the Mediterranean to North Africa, then the whole length of Africa through eighteen countries, from the Sahara and the Nile to the Rift Valley and the Cape.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Long Way Down","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_Way_Down"}],"approximate":"Countries, key places and dates follow public accounts; the exact roads between them are approximate.","km":20790,"bbox":[-4.3672,-34.833,39.1476,58.6373],"stops":[{"name":"John o' Groats","place":"John o' Groats","at":[58.6373,-3.0689],"date":"12 May 2007","text":"The start at the northern tip of mainland Britain, with Cape Town about 24,000 km away.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Duncansby_Head_lighthouse.JPG/500px-Duncansby_Head_lighthouse.JPG","page":"Duncansby Head","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Duncansby_Head_lighthouse.JPG","credit":"Russ McLean at English Wikipedia","license":"CC BY 3.0"}},{"name":"Crieff","place":"Crieff, Scotland","at":[56.3727,-3.8397],"text":"A night at the McGregor family home in Perthshire on the way south.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Heading_east_on_Crieff%27s_High_Street_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3152513.jpg/500px-Heading_east_on_Crieff%27s_High_Street_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3152513.jpg","page":"Crieff","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heading_east_on_Crieff%27s_High_Street_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3152513.jpg","credit":"jim and liz denham","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Silverstone","place":"Silverstone Circuit","at":[52.0718,-1.0143],"text":"Camping in the middle of the famous race circuit."},{"name":"London","place":"Shepherd's Bush, London","at":[51.5053,-0.223],"text":"Back through London before leaving Britain.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/London_Skyline_%28125508655%29.jpeg/500px-London_Skyline_%28125508655%29.jpeg","page":"London","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:London_Skyline_%28125508655%29.jpeg","credit":"Ilya Grigorik","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Calais","place":"Calais, France","at":[50.9525,1.8538],"text":"Under the Channel by train, then south through France.","by":"train","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/TGV_TMST_3011-2_-_Sortie_Tunnel_sous_la_Manche_%C3%A0_Coquelles.jpg/500px-TGV_TMST_3011-2_-_Sortie_Tunnel_sous_la_Manche_%C3%A0_Coquelles.jpg","page":"Channel Tunnel","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TGV_TMST_3011-2_-_Sortie_Tunnel_sous_la_Manche_%C3%A0_Coquelles.jpg","credit":"Billy69150 (voir les conditions d'utilisation / see licensing below)","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Sicily","place":"Palermo, Italy","at":[38.1112,13.3524],"text":"Down the length of Italy to Sicily, the end of the European leg.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Sicilia_Palermo5_tango7174.jpg/500px-Sicilia_Palermo5_tango7174.jpg","page":"Palermo","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sicilia_Palermo5_tango7174.jpg","credit":"Tango7174","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Tunis","place":"Tunis, Tunisia","at":[36.8002,10.1858],"text":"A ferry across the Mediterranean to Africa.","by":"ferry","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/TunisAveHabibBourguiba.jpg/500px-TunisAveHabibBourguiba.jpg","page":"Tunis","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TunisAveHabibBourguiba.jpg","credit":"Dacoslett","license":"CC0"}},{"name":"Matmata","place":"Matmata, Tunisia","at":[33.5457,9.9671],"text":"The underground Berber homes of Matmata, used as Luke Skywalker's home in Star Wars. A treat for the man who played Obi-Wan.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Matmata%2C_Tunisia.JPG/500px-Matmata%2C_Tunisia.JPG","page":"Matmata, Tunisia","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matmata%2C_Tunisia.JPG","credit":"Damien slattery Photographed by Colin Kenworthy","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Tripoli","place":"Tripoli, Libya","at":[32.8967,13.1778],"text":"Into Libya along the coast. Two of the crew couldn't get visas and had to fly round to Egypt.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Al-Saraya_al-Hamra_Fortress%2C_Tripoli_%285282695461%29.jpg/500px-Al-Saraya_al-Hamra_Fortress%2C_Tripoli_%285282695461%29.jpg","page":"Red Castle of Tripoli","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Al-Saraya_al-Hamra_Fortress%2C_Tripoli_%285282695461%29.jpg","credit":"David Stanley from Nanaimo, Canada","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Benghazi","place":"Benghazi, Libya","at":[32.12,20.0812],"text":"Long, hot desert days along the Gulf of Sidra.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Al_Daawa_alIslamiyah2.JPG/500px-Al_Daawa_alIslamiyah2.JPG","page":"Benghazi","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Al_Daawa_alIslamiyah2.JPG","credit":"Maher A. A. Abdussalam","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Pyramids of Giza","place":"Giza, Egypt","at":[29.9871,31.2118],"text":"The pyramids, then south along the Nile.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Pyramids_of_the_Giza_Necropolis.jpg/500px-Pyramids_of_the_Giza_Necropolis.jpg","page":"Giza pyramid complex","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pyramids_of_the_Giza_Necropolis.jpg","credit":"KennyOMG","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Luxor","place":"Luxor, Egypt","at":[25.7021,32.6472],"text":"Temples of ancient Thebes on the Nile.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Temple_de_Louxor_68.jpg/500px-Temple_de_Louxor_68.jpg","page":"Karnak","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Temple_de_Louxor_68.jpg","credit":"René Hourdry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Aswan","place":"Aswan, Egypt","at":[24.0911,32.8973],"text":"The end of the road south in Egypt: from here the way to Sudan is by boat.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Panoramic_view_of_Aswan%2C_Egypt.jpg/500px-Panoramic_view_of_Aswan%2C_Egypt.jpg","page":"Aswan","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panoramic_view_of_Aswan%2C_Egypt.jpg","credit":"Vyacheslav Argenberg","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Wadi Halfa","place":"Wadi Halfa, Sudan","at":[21.8005,31.3507],"text":"The ferry down Lake Nasser into Sudan.","by":"ferry","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Lake_Nasser_Vista.jpg/500px-Lake_Nasser_Vista.jpg","page":"Lake Nasser","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lake_Nasser_Vista.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Khartoum","place":"Khartoum, Sudan","at":[15.5636,32.5349],"text":"Desert tracks and heat to where the Blue and White Nile meet.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/%C2%A9Nile-Project_-Sari_Omer_0025.jpg/500px-%C2%A9Nile-Project_-Sari_Omer_0025.jpg","page":"Khartoum","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C2%A9Nile-Project_-Sari_Omer_0025.jpg","credit":"Evon2023","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Gondar","place":"Gondar, Ethiopia","at":[12.6104,37.4668],"text":"Up into the Ethiopian highlands: green mountains, castles and crowds of children by the road.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Gonder_from_the_Goha_hotel.jpg/500px-Gonder_from_the_Goha_hotel.jpg","page":"Gondar","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gonder_from_the_Goha_hotel.jpg","credit":"Giustino","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Addis Ababa","place":"Addis Ababa, Ethiopia","at":[9.0358,38.7524],"text":"Ethiopia's capital, high in the mountains.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Addis_in_night.jpg/500px-Addis_in_night.jpg","page":"Addis Ababa","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Addis_in_night.jpg","credit":"Abshewaga","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Moyale","place":"Moyale, Kenya","at":[3.5159,39.0584],"text":"The border into Kenya, and the start of a notorious stretch of rough, rocky road south."},{"name":"Marsabit","place":"Marsabit, Kenya","at":[2.3381,37.9916],"text":"Through the remote north of Kenya on dirt and rocks.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Marsabit-Moyale_Rd.jpg/500px-Marsabit-Moyale_Rd.jpg","page":"Marsabit","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marsabit-Moyale_Rd.jpg","credit":"Lindsey Nicholson","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"The equator","place":"Nanyuki, Kenya","at":[0.014,37.0746],"text":"Crossing the equator near Mount Kenya: into the southern hemisphere.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Nanyuki_main_street.jpg/500px-Nanyuki_main_street.jpg","page":"Nanyuki","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nanyuki_main_street.jpg","credit":"Christiaan Kooyman","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Kampala","place":"Kampala, Uganda","at":[0.3177,32.5814],"text":"West into Uganda and its green hills.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Urban_Rising%2C_KAMPALA%2C_Uganda.jpg/500px-Urban_Rising%2C_KAMPALA%2C_Uganda.jpg","page":"Kampala","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Urban_Rising%2C_KAMPALA%2C_Uganda.jpg","credit":"Chapelle musa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Kigali","place":"Kigali, Rwanda","at":[-1.9534,30.114],"text":"Rwanda, where they met President Paul Kagame.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/High_Angle_View_Of_Kigali_City_Street_on_November_29%2C_2018._Emmanuel_Kwizera.jpg/500px-High_Angle_View_Of_Kigali_City_Street_on_November_29%2C_2018._Emmanuel_Kwizera.jpg","page":"Kigali","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:High_Angle_View_Of_Kigali_City_Street_on_November_29%2C_2018._Emmanuel_Kwizera.jpg","credit":"Emmanuelkwizera","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Arusha","place":"Arusha, Tanzania","at":[-3.3697,36.6881],"text":"Tanzania, between Kilimanjaro and the great parks of the north.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Arusha_City_view.jpg/500px-Arusha_City_view.jpg","page":"Arusha","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arusha_City_view.jpg","credit":"Halidtz","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Malawi","place":"Lilongwe, Malawi","at":[-13.9875,33.7681],"text":"Malawi, where Ewan's wife Eve joined the ride.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Lake_Malawi_seen_from_orbit.jpg/500px-Lake_Malawi_seen_from_orbit.jpg","page":"Lake Malawi","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lake_Malawi_seen_from_orbit.jpg","credit":"National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA)","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Lusaka","place":"Lusaka, Zambia","at":[-15.4163,28.2818],"text":"South-west across Zambia.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Downtown_Lusaka.JPG/500px-Downtown_Lusaka.JPG","page":"Lusaka","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Downtown_Lusaka.JPG","credit":"Matthew Grollnek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Victoria Falls","place":"Livingstone, Zambia","at":[-17.8531,25.8614],"text":"The smoke that thunders, on the Zambezi.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Cataratas_Victoria%2C_Zambia-Zimbabue%2C_2018-07-27%2C_DD_04.jpg/500px-Cataratas_Victoria%2C_Zambia-Zimbabue%2C_2018-07-27%2C_DD_04.jpg","page":"Victoria Falls","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cataratas_Victoria%2C_Zambia-Zimbabue%2C_2018-07-27%2C_DD_04.jpg","credit":"Diego Delso","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Botswana","place":"Maun, Botswana","at":[-19.9861,23.4224],"text":"The edge of the Okavango Delta and the Kalahari.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Okavango_Delta%2C_Botswana1.jpg/500px-Okavango_Delta%2C_Botswana1.jpg","page":"Okavango Delta","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Okavango_Delta%2C_Botswana1.jpg","credit":"Joachim Huber","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Namibia","place":"Windhoek, Namibia","at":[-22.5776,17.0773],"text":"Gravel roads through Namibia's huge, empty desert landscapes.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Namib_desert_MODIS.jpg/500px-Namib_desert_MODIS.jpg","page":"Namib","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Namib_desert_MODIS.jpg","credit":"Jeff Schmaltz, MODIS Land Rapid Response Team, NASA GSFC","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Cape Agulhas","place":"Cape Agulhas, South Africa","at":[-34.8333,19.9999],"text":"The southernmost point of Africa, where the Atlantic and Indian oceans meet."},{"name":"Cape Town","place":"Cape Town, South Africa","at":[-33.9288,18.4172],"date":"4 Aug 2007","text":"The finish, escorted into Cape Town by a crowd of local riders.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Camps_bay_%2853460319478%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Camps_bay_%2853460319478%29_%28cropped%29.jpg","page":"Cape Town","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Camps_bay_%2853460319478%29_%28cropped%29.jpg","credit":"Der Berzerker from Washington, DC, USA","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}}],"legs":[{"by":"ride","km":383,"line":[[58.6373,-3.0689],[58.6048,-3.0885],[58.5734,-3.0725],[58.5081,-3.1528],[58.476,-3.1445],[58.4427,-3.092],[58.3485,-3.1611],[58.3112,-3.2186],[58.3102,-3.2784],[58.276,-3.3892],[58.2145,-3.4793],[58.1842,-3.4964],[58.1628,-3.5857],[58.102,-3.6731],[58.0694,-3.791],[57.9891,-3.8971],[57.9512,-4.0825],[57.9089,-4.0562],[57.8749,-4.1102],[57.8358,-4.1098],[57.7938,-4.0